    "findings": [
      "Saltwind town v2 has a wide auburn-roof market and dense connected stilt/quay buildings with substantial lower body mass. The tall flag from v1 is gone; it now reads as an enclosed trading town rather than a village-sized cluster under a pole.",
      "Wardhall town v2 has a broad low wall enclosure, a central market/work hall and a dense group of surrounding workshops. Its building count and enclosed footprint exceed the three-house village; its lower roofline deliberately avoids competing with the 128px towered city.",
      "Town native canvases remain 96x96, villages 96x96 and cities 128x128. No enlarged town runtime contract, copied village upgrade, fake animation, or changed atlas publication is introduced.",
      "Original source margins are genuinely transparent and the full alpha>=128 silhouette is retained. Actual bounds are recorded; the generator did not satisfy the requested 15% side-margin preference, but neither silhouette touches an edge and preparation retains safe native padding.",
      "Root independent reviewer retains final approval and in-game contrast/progression judgment. Other twenty-eight role candidates were not regenerated or reprocessed."
    ]
